*.sh text eol=lf

# The docs/cljs playground bundles are committed, vendored prebuilts that
# esbuild / shadow-cljs emit with LF endings (rf2-ee38b.22). Pin LF so a
# Windows checkout / rebuild never CRLF-normalises them — that would make the
# CI bundle-drift gate (tools-playground) `git diff` against a fresh Linux
# build spuriously fail.
docs/cljs/playground.js text eol=lf
docs/cljs/playground-rf2.js text eol=lf
docs/cljs/playground.css text eol=lf
# Pin the source CSS to LF too: `copy-css.mjs` copies it byte-for-byte to the
# committed docs/cljs/playground.css, so a CRLF source would yield a CRLF
# output and trip the drift gate.
docs/tools/playground/src/playground.css text eol=lf
